# Harness SDD — project instructions

## Session start (mandatory)

1. Run `./check.sh --quiet`. If it fails, stop and fix the environment.
2. Run `./.agents/bootstrap.sh brief` for the active feature, its next task,
   and the session state. Do not read `feature_list.json` or progress logs in full.
3. Load anything else only when the task needs it; `AGENTS.md §2` says when.

## Hard rules

- One feature in `in_progress` at a time.
- `sdd: true` features: spec → human approval → implement → review → done.
- Never edit the approved spec. Every R<n> ends with at least one test.
- `./check.sh` must pass before a feature is `done`.
- Never edit generated files (`CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/`); edit `.agents/` and re-render.

